draw((3,2)--(4,4)--(5,2));
[/asy]

In the ﬁgure on the right,  $O$  is the center of the circle,  $OK$  and  $OA$  are perpendicular to one another,  $M$  is the midpoint of  $OK$ ,  $BN$   is parallel to  $OK$ , and  $\angle AMN=\angle NMO$ . Determine the measure of  $\angle A B N$  in degrees.

[asy]
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10));
pair O=origin, A=dir(90), K=dir(180), M=0.5*dir(180), N=2/5*dir(90), B=dir(degrees((2/5, sqrt(21/25)))+90);
